# Commit Trailers

When creating git commits in this project, ALWAYS append these trailers at the end of the commit message body:

```
Signed-off-by: Enric Balletbo i Serra <eballetbo@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Cursor:claude-4.6-opus
```

## Rules

- NEVER use `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- ALWAYS include `Signed-off-by` with the author's identity
- ALWAYS include `Assisted-by: AGENT_NAME:MODEL_VERSION` (currently `Cursor:claude-4.6-opus`)
- Trailers go after a blank line at the end of the commit body
- `Signed-off-by` comes before `Assisted-by`

## Example

```
feat(text): add blinking cursor during editing

Implements a visible blinking cursor at the insertion point
when editing text.

Signed-off-by: Enric Balletbo i Serra <eballetbo@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Cursor:claude-4.6-opus
```
